            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0557" n="543" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg543"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9–244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-02T15:00:00+07:00">September 2,
                            1944—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 2—2:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1489. Plenary Session of People’s Political Council is scheduled at Chungking
                    starting September 5th. It is reported main topics of discussion will include
                    army reforms, educational improvements and implementation of democracy. It is
                    understood Communist delegates in Chungking plan to participate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
